[{"code":"top_level_record_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":19,"col":11},"end":{"line":19,"col":29}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL RECORD CHANGED","message":"`{ origin | x = n }` changes `Main.origin` itself, but it is `origin`, a\ntop-level value.\n\n19|moved n = { origin | x = n }\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the record is changed in place here\n\n15|origin = { x = 0, y = 0 }\n   ^^^^^^ the top-level record is defined here\n\nA top-level value is shared by every part of the program and never changes:\nchanged in place, it would change for every part that reads it.\n\nMake `origin` a function that builds a fresh record at each call, `origin ⊤`, or\nchange a copy: `{ Record.copy origin | … }`.\n\nThis is the language's rule for top-level values, whether or not anything else\nreads the record (ownership-checker.md §31.4)."}]
